### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains HTTP client.
@base = http://localhost:4000/api/v1

### Register (returns an accessToken)
POST {{base}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.com", "password": "password123", "teamName": "My Team" }

### Login
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.com", "password": "password123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Who am I?
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create an endpoint to monitor
POST {{base}}/endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Example API",
  "url": "https://httpbin.org/status/200",
  "intervalSeconds": 60,
  "timeoutMs": 10000,
  "expectedStatus": "200",
  "failureThreshold": 3
}

### List endpoints
GET {{base}}/endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Check it right now (returns the result)
@endpointId = paste-an-id-here
POST {{base}}/endpoints/{{endpointId}}/check-now
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recent check history
GET {{base}}/endpoints/{{endpointId}}/checks?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Point an endpoint at the mock target (run: npm run mock)
POST {{base}}/endpoints
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mock switch", "url": "http://localhost:5001/switch", "intervalSeconds": 30, "failureThreshold": 2 }
